### Domain Feature UI Routes Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000/domain

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/domain
@domainId = 123
@domain = example.com

### 1. Get User Domains
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Get User Active Domains
GET {{baseUrl}}/active
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 3. Add Domain
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "{{domain}}"
}

###

### 4. Add Custom Domain
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "mycustomdomain.com"
}

###

### 5. Add Subdomain
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "subdomain.example.com"
}

###

### 6. Refresh Domain
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{domainId}}/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 7. Delete Domain
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{domainId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 8. Test with Invalid Domain Format (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "invalid-domain-format"
}

###

### 9. Test with Blocked Domain (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": "google.com"
}

###

### 10. Test with Empty Domain (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "domain": ""
}

###

### 11. Test with Invalid Domain ID (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/invalid-id/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 12. Test Delete with Invalid Domain ID (should fail)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/invalid-id
Content-Type: application/json

###
